    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/06E60EB4A3425A1B8B2E3A5F3F1E2A6F/jobs/310266": {
      "title": "Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Admissions Counselor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Admissions Counselor Lynchburg  - Lynchburg, VA 24501 Apply Overview Salary Range $20.77 Hourly Position Type Staff Job Shift Full time Education Level 4 Year Degree Apply Description Admissions Counselor The University of Lynchburg , a private, regional university in the beautiful foothills of the Blue Ridge Mountains in Central Virginia, is seeking applicants for full-time, Admissions Counselor position in Undergraduate Admissions. This position reports to, is supervised by, and evaluated by the Director of Admissions. The evaluation of work performance will be ongoing and will be carried out by the Admissions Counselor. It will include the specific duties and responsibilities of this position description plus employee attitude and general working behavior. Job Type : FT (Benefits Eligible) Job Purpose: The primary focus of the Admissions Counselor is to build strong, lasting relationships with prospective students, guiding and supporting them through every stage of the college choice process—including program selection, application completion, admission evaluation, financial aid navigation, and final enrollment. Representing the institution to prospective students, families, high school guidance counselors, and community organizations, this position executes data-informed territory recruitment plans to contribute directly to institutional enrollment goals. Specific Job Duties: Territory Management & Strategy: Plan, manage, and execute targeted recruitment strategies within an assigned geographic territory to meet individual inquiry, applicant, and enrollment goals. Develop and maintain territory data to inform strategic travel itineraries and outreach plans. Multi-Channel Student Outreach: Utilize phone, email, text messaging, and social media outreach proactively to cultivate personalized relationships with prospective students and families, guiding them from inquiry to matriculation. Application Review & Admissions Decisions: Review candidate application files thoroughly, evaluate transcripts and credentials, and render admissions decisions in compliance with institutional standards. CRM Workflow & Data Tracking (Slate): Manage prospective student records in Slate CRM. Record all conversations, campus touchpoints, and recruitment interactions to drive personalized communication workflows and yield tracking. Campus Visits, Presentations & On-Campus Interviews: Conduct individual student/family interviews, deliver engaging group presentations, and lead information sessions for visiting students, families, and college counseling personnel. Event Participation & Field Recruitment: Represent the institution at on-campus and off-campus recruitment events, college fairs, high school visits, and community outreach programs. Counselor & Community Relationship Building: Develop long-standing relationships with high school counselors and community-based organizations (CBOs), designing collaborative opportunities to bring students and advisors to campus. Special Project Ownership & Operational Support: Manage or oversee a specialized operational project (e.g., Student Ambassador leadership, campus tour program management, digital outreach initiatives, or transfer credit liaison work) to support enrollment goals. Committee Governance & Professional Development: Serve on campus committees related to student development (orientation, leadership, retention). Participate in national/regional professional organizations (e.g., NACAC, SACAC/VACAC) for continuous development. Basic Financial Aid & Affordability Counseling: Guiding prospective students and families through FAFSA completion steps, merit scholarship qualifications, and cost of attendance estimates. Targeted Yield & Conversion Campaign Execution: Executing phone marathons, admitted student outreach campaigns, and personalized decision follow-ups during peak yield season. Transfer & Diversity Pipeline Support: Partnering with community colleges and access organizations to expand non-traditional and underrepresented student recruitment. Other duties as assigned Starting Salary: $20.77 per hour Benefits: Generous paid vacation, personal days, paid sick time and family leave, comprehensive insurance (medical, dental, vision, etc.) and retirement plans, flexible spending account, tuition remission, life and long-term disability insurance, and more. Learn more about employment benefits at the University of Lynchburg. Schedule: 8:30 am - 5:00 pm (7.5 hours/day with some evenings and weekends to meet needs of the department may be required Qualifications Experience/Skills: Ability to communicate effectively and have the ability to understand, comprehend and follow directions Must have good teamwork skills Ability to write effectively Exceptional attention to details Strong proofreading skills Comfortable delivering presentations to small and large groups Physical Demands: Prolonged standing/sitting/wrist movement Long periods sitting in front of a computer screen Time spent traveling in motor vehicles/flights to and from recruitment events Limited lifting and carrying of luggage and recruitment collateral Ability to lift 20 lbs. Required Qualifications: 1-2 years of professional experience in sales, marketing recruitment, higher education, coaching, or another goal-oriented field Valid Drivers License Extensive travel required Education: Bachelor's Degree Work Remotely: No We seek candidates who are committed to the University of Lynchburg’s efforts to create an environment that fosters a student-centered environment, develops the breadth of knowledge associated with liberal education, respects and supports diversity, equity, and inclusion, values and celebrates diverse faith traditions, and sustains close working relationships among faculty, staff, students, alumni, and community partners. Candidates must successfully pass a background check that is satisfactory to the University. Submit a cover letter, résumé, and three professional references to: Human Resources Jobs Page The University of Lynchburg is dedicated to inclusive excellence. We celebrate the diversity of our common life, affirming our different histories, realities, and identities. All belong here. As a testament to our strong commitment to accessibility, diversity, and inclusion, we will attract, celebrate, and retain a community of diverse students, staff, and faculty; foster belonging; and create a campus environment that embraces civil discourse and accountability for our words and actions. The University of Lynchburg embraces diversity in its broadest sense. We will cultivate an inclusive, equitable, and safe campus climate grounded in mutual respect and understanding, where all members of our diverse learning community - alumni, employees, learners, visitors, and volunteers- can thrive. The University of Lynchburg is an equal-opportunity employer. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/06E60EB4A3425A1B8B2E3A5F3F1E2A6F/jobs/310248": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Psychological Science",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Psychological Science You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant/Associate Professor of Psychological Science Lynchburg  - Lynchburg, VA 24501 Apply Overview Salary Range $62,000.00 - $68,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Faculty Job Shift Full time Education Level Graduate Degree Apply Description Assistant or Associate Professor in Psychological Science The University of Lynchburg , a private, regional university in the beautiful foothills of the Blue Ridge Mountains in Central Virginia, is seeking applicants for two tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor positions in Psychological Science beginning in the 2027-28 academic year. We seek colleagues with a strong commitment to teaching excellence and scholarship. Area of specialization is open, but we prefer candidates with expertise in clinical/counseling and social/cognitive psychology. Candidates will have the opportunity to take advantage of resources provided by the Teaching and Learning Center and the Percy Wootton Research Center and will be eligible to apply for internal funds to support travel, scholarly work, faculty-student research, and professional development. Specific Job Duties: Teaching a combination of introductory and upper-level courses. Courses in the regular rotation include introductory psychology, research design and analysis, senior capstone, and courses in the candidate’s area of specialization. Typical teaching load is four courses per semester. Collaboration with colleagues on curriculum development, undergraduate academic advising, and service on University committees. Supervising student research projects and engaging in scholarly activity. Benefits: Generous sick time and family leave, comprehensive insurance (medical, dental, vision, etc.) and retirement plans, flexible spending account, tuition remission, life and long term disability insurance, and more. Learn more about employment benefits at the University of Lynchburg . Teaching Load: The normal teaching load is 12 hours per semester. Physical Demands: Prolonged periods standing or sitting at a desk. Qualifications Required Qualifications/Education: A PhD or PsyD in Psychology by August 2027. Open area of specialization but expertise in clinical/counseling and social/cognitive psychology is preferred. Previous undergraduate teaching experience is preferred. Familiarity with quantitative research methodologies. A primary interest in teaching and mentoring undergraduate research at a liberal arts institution is required. Work Remotely: No Candidates may show interest in this position by submitting the following to the Human Resources Jobs Page : A completed application; A current curriculum vitae (CV) or resume; and A single document containing the following: cover letter, a statement of your teaching philosophy including evidence of teaching effectiveness, a research statement describing past and present research projects, your unofficial graduate transcripts (official transcripts required for employment), and the names and contact information for three professional references. Questions can be directed to the department chair of Psychological Science, Dr. Alisha Marciano ( marciano.a@lynchburg.edu ) Review of applications and materials will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. The selected candidate must successfully complete a background check that is satisfactory to the University. During the application review process, candidates may be asked to provide the following: Graduate and undergraduate transcripts (unofficial transcripts accepted; however, official transcripts are required upon an offer and acceptance of position) Names and contact information for three professional references The University of Lynchburg is dedicated to inclusive excellence. We celebrate the diversity of our common life, affirming our different histories, realities, and identities. All belong here. As a testament to our strong commitment to accessibility, diversity, and inclusion, we will attract, celebrate, and retain a community of diverse students, staff, and faculty; foster belonging; and create a campus environment that embraces civil discourse and accountability for our words and actions. The University of Lynchburg embraces diversity in its broadest sense. We will cultivate an inclusive, equitable, and safe campus climate grounded in mutual respect and understanding, where all members of our diverse learning community - alumni, employees, learners, visitors, and volunteers- can thrive. The University of Lynchburg is an equal-opportunity employer. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/06E60EB4A3425A1B8B2E3A5F3F1E2A6F/jobs/310112": {
      "title": "Department Chair and Associate or Full Professor of Computer Science",
      "description": "Department Chair and Associate or Full Professor of Computer Science You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Department Chair and Associate or Full Professor of Computer Science Lynchburg  - Lynchburg, VA 24501 Apply Overview Salary Range $90,000.00 - $117,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Faculty Job Shift Full time Education Level Graduate Degree Apply Description Department Chair and Associate or Full Professor of Computer Science The University of Lynchburg invites applications for an innovative, future-focused leader to serve as Department Chair and Tenure-Track Associate or Full Professor of Computer Science beginning in the 2027-28 academic year. As the tech sector undergoes a paradigm shift toward integrated intelligence, the era of the isolated syntax specialist is giving way to the age of system designers, AI architects, and ethical technology leaders. The University of Lynchburg seeks a visionary educator-scholar who will lead our Computer Science program away from language-centric coding and toward a human-centered, interdisciplinary model rooted in the liberal arts. We seek an academic intrapreneur who recognizes that a midsize private university's competitive advantage lies in agility, cross-pollination, and high-touch mentorship. The successful candidate will articulate a clear ROI to students and families by positioning our Computer Science degree as AI-proof--emphasizing high-level logic, ethical judgment, domain expertise, and system architecture that technology cannot replace. The Chair will be expected to lead comprehensive curriculum reform, foster strategic enrollment growth, cultivate external community and business partnerships, and ensure the career readiness of our graduates. The ideal candidate has a forward-thinking vision for the future of Computer Science education and will thrive in a teaching-focused liberal arts environment. They remain current in their field and have industry experience to back up their academic credentials. Leadership experience in academia or industry is essential, ideally experience leading change management initiatives and/or significant program creation or reform. We seek a collaborative builder with an innovative product manager mindset. Specific Job Duties: Serve as the strategic architect of the Computer Science program, transforming traditional curriculum into a versatile, future-focused pathway that integrates human-led AI literacy across disciplines. Lead a comprehensive curricular update that shifts focus from syntax-focused programming to computational thinking, system architecture, machine learning operations, and cloud architecture. Integrate AI ethics and human-centered design into foundational coursework. Develop interdisciplinary degree pathways and minors in collaboration with disciplines across campus. Re-envision assessment practices to include team-based product sprints and client-facing projects that solve real-world problems for local businesses and non-profits. Help students bridge the entry-level hiring gap by creating opportunities for them to articulate their experience and skills. Cultivate local and regional corporate, civic, and non-profit connections to secure project pipelines, internship opportunities, and job prospects. Oversee departmental operations, budgets, course scheduling, program assessment, and faculty development. Drive marketing, recruiting, and retention efforts in the department, at campus events, and online. Maintain a reduced teaching load (commensurate with administrative duties as Chair) delivering core and advanced Computer Science courses. Benefits: Generous sick time and family leave, comprehensive insurance (medical, dental, vision, etc.) and retirement plans, flexible spending account, tuition remission, life and long-term disability insurance, and more. Learn more about employment benefits at the University of Lynchburg. Teaching Load: The typical full-time faculty teaching load is 12 contact hours per semester, reduced for this role to accommodate departmental leadership and administrative responsibilities. Salary: 90,000-$117,000. Salary and rank are commensurate with education and experience Physical Demands: Prolonged periods standing or sitting at a desk Qualifications Required Qualifications/Education: A PhD in Computer Science, Data Science, Systems Engineering, or a closely related computational field required by the start date. Demonstrated record of teaching excellence and curriculum development. 2+ years of leadership experience in industry or higher education. A clear vision for Computer Science education within a liberal arts framework, with demonstrated commitment to human-centered AI, system architecture, and interdisciplinary collaboration. A passion for high-touch undergraduate mentorship, project-based learning, and building industry/community partnership Preferred Qualifications: 3+ years of professional industry, consulting, or software architecture experience alongside academic credentials. Demonstrated success leading academic change management, curriculum redesign, or launching new interdisciplinary academic programs. A proven track record of securing external corporate, civic, or grant partnerships that yield student internships, client projects, or seed funding. Demonstrated ability to communicate the strategic value and career ROI of a liberal arts-grounded technical degree to prospective students, parents, and external stakeholders. Work Remotely: No Candidates may show interest in this position by submitting to the Human Resources Jobs Page . Applications should include: A completed application in Paycom A cover letter detailing your vision for leading a future-focused Computer Science program within a liberal arts university. A current curriculum vitae (CV) or resume A statement of teaching philosophy and curriculum innovation Unofficial graduate transcripts (official transcripts will be requested later) Names and contact information for three professional references Questions about this position can be directed to Melissa Brooks, Administrative Coordinator, School of Liberal Arts & Sciences ( brooks_ms@lynchburg.edu ). Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. The selected candidate must successfully complete a background check satisfactory to the University. The University of Lynchburg is dedicated to inclusive excellence. We celebrate the diversity of our common life, affirming our different histories, realities, and identities. All belong here. As a testament to our strong commitment to accessibility, diversity, and inclusion, we will attract, celebrate, and retain a community of diverse students, staff, and faculty; foster belonging; and create a campus environment that embraces civil discourse and accountability for our words and actions. The University of Lynchburg embraces diversity in its broadest sense. We will cultivate an inclusive, equitable, and safe campus climate grounded in mutual respect and understanding, where all members of our diverse learning community - alumni, employees, learners, visitors, and volunteers- can thrive. The University of Lynchburg is an equal-opportunity employer. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/06E60EB4A3425A1B8B2E3A5F3F1E2A6F/jobs/308715": {
      "title": "Event Specialist",
      "description": "Event Specialist You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Event Specialist Lynchburg  - Lynchburg, VA 24501 Apply Overview Salary Range $16.50 Hourly Position Type Staff Job Shift Full time Education Level High School Apply Description The University of Lynchburg , a private, regional university in the beautiful foothills of the Blue Ridge Mountains in Central Virginia, is seeking applicants for an Event Specialist position in the Catering Department for the Finance and Operations division. This position reports to, is supervised by, and evaluated by the Manager of Catering and Events. The evaluation of work performance will be ongoing and will be carried out by the Manager of Catering and Events. It will include the specific duties and responsibilities of this position description plus employee attitude and general working behavior. Job Summary The Catering & Events Specialist oversees daily event operations within the department to ensure staff productivity, quality service delivery, and compliance with university policies. This hands-on, full-time role plans and executes events within financial and time constraints while ensuring guest satisfaction and facilitating university business objectives. The specialist works closely with supervisors, event staff, vendors, and campus departments to deliver exceptional experiences across all university events. ESSENTIAL DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES Review event BEOs (Banquet Event Orders) to fully understand guest expectations and specific AV and catering requirements. Set up and calibrate AV equipment, including microphones, mixers, speakers, and projectors, prior to event start times. Conduct pre-event \"sound checks\" and equipment testing to ensure seamless audiovisual functionality. Troubleshoot AV technical issues in real-time during live events to minimize interruptions and ensure guest satisfaction. Execute room setups according to floor diagrams, ensuring proper table spacing, chair placement, and equipment layout. Coordinate efficient \"room flips\" between consecutive event sessions to maintain event timelines. Assist the catering team with buffet table setup, ensuring food displays are aesthetically pleasing and appropriately labeled. Provide active catering support, including the timely replenishment of buffet lines and tray passing. Conduct efficient service clearing and busing to maintain a clean and professional event environment. Monitor food temperatures and quality throughout the duration of the event, reporting issues to the culinary team immediately. Act as the primary point of contact for external vendors, assisting them with load-in, setup, and load-out logistics. Guide and supervise student workers and temporary service staff to ensure consistent adherence to service standards. Enforce workplace safety and sanitation guidelines to maintain a secure environment for all guests and staff. Perform thorough post-event tear-downs, ensuring all furniture, AV equipment, and catering supplies are cleaned and properly stored. Participate in post-event evaluations to identify successes and opportunities for improvement in future event execution. Maintain the cleanliness and organization of back-of-house storage areas and dedicated AV equipment lockers. Facilitate constant communication between the kitchen and floor staff to ensure synchronized food service and AV delivery. Manage the inventory of AV cables, adapters, and catering service supplies, reporting needed repairs or shortages to the supervisor. Starting Salary: $16.50 an hour Benefits: Generous paid vacation, personal days, paid sick time and family leave, comprehensive insurance (medical, dental, vision, etc.) and retirement plans, flexible spending account, tuition remission, life and long-term disability insurance, and more. Learn more about employment benefits at the University of Lynchburg. Schedule: Evenings and weekends to meet needs of the department may be required Qualifications Experience/Skills: Self-Starter: Ability to follow instructions and execute tasks with minimal direct supervision. Hands-on Hospitality Knowledge: Understanding of event setups, banquet operations, catering service flows, and basic hospitality standards. Adaptable Communication: Strong verbal communication skills to effectively direct staff, assist clients, and coordinate with culinary/tech teams. Multitasking & Problem Solving: Calm under pressure with the ability to handle live event adjustments smoothly. Basic Technical/AV Aptitude: Comfortable managing basic event tech (microphones, background audio, basic display screens) as needed on the floor. Physical Demands: Heavy standing and walking for extended periods. Frequent lifting, carrying, push/pulling up to 50 lbs. unassisted (tables, chairs, catering carts, staging). Indoor and outdoor event setups across varying weather conditions. Qualifications: 2+ years of experience in hospitality, banquet operations, catering service or event support. Valid driver's license with personal transportation Ability to operate utility/golf carts and event equipment safely Work Remotely: No We seek candidates who are committed to the University of Lynchburg’s efforts to create an environment that fosters a student-centered environment, develops the breadth of knowledge associated with liberal education, respects and supports diversity, equity, and inclusion, values and celebrates diverse faith traditions, and sustains close working relationships among faculty, staff, students, alumni, and community partners. Candidates must successfully pass a background check that is satisfactory to the University. Submit a cover letter, résumé, and three professional references to: Human Resources Jobs Page The University of Lynchburg is dedicated to inclusive excellence. We celebrate the diversity of our common life, affirming our different histories, realities, and identities. All belong here. As a testament to our strong commitment to accessibility, diversity, and inclusion, we will attract, celebrate, and retain a community of diverse students, staff, and faculty; foster belonging; and create a campus environment that embraces civil discourse and accountability for our words and actions. The University of Lynchburg embraces diversity in its broadest sense. We will cultivate an inclusive, equitable, and safe campus climate grounded in mutual respect and understanding, where all members of our diverse learning community - alumni, employees, learners, visitors, and volunteers- can thrive. The University of Lynchburg is an equal-opportunity employer. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/06E60EB4A3425A1B8B2E3A5F3F1E2A6F/jobs/307576": {
      "title": "Administrative Coordinator, MPAM and School of Medicine and Health Sciences",
      "description": "Administrative Coordinator, MPAM and School of Medicine and Health Sciences You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Administrative Coordinator, MPAM and School of Medicine and Health Sciences Lynchburg  - Lynchburg, VA 24501 Apply Overview Salary Range $35,000.00 - $42,000.00 Salary Position Type Staff Job Shift Day Education Level 4 Year Degree Apply Description Administrative Coordinator, MPAM and School of Medicine and Health Sciences The University of Lynchburg , a private, regional university in the beautiful foothills of the Blue Ridge Mountains in Central Virginia, is seeking applicants for an Administrative Coordinator position for the Dean and Associate Dean of the School of Medicine and Health Sciences and support for SMHS faculty with a focus on the Doctor of Executive Leadership department. This position reports to and is supervised by the Dean and Associate Dean of the School of Medicine and Health Sciences. Performance will be evaluated on an ongoing basis and through the University's established performance evaluation process. Evaluation will be based on the successful execution of the duties and responsibilities outlined in this position description, quality and timeliness of work, communication and collaboration, professionalism, and overall job performance. Job Type : FT/RPT (Benefits Eligible) Job Purpose: The Administrative Coordinator serves a dual role supporting the Dean's Office of the School of Medicine and Health Sciences and the Doctor of Executive Leadership (DEL) program. The position provides high-level administrative support to school leadership while coordinating the daily administrative operations of the DEL program. Responsibilities include supporting faculty and students, managing communications and records, coordinating meetings and events, assisting with budgeting, reporting, and accreditation activities, and ensuring efficient administrative operations across the School and program. Specific Job Duties: School of Medicine and Health Sciences Provides high-level administrative support to the Dean and Associate Dean of the School of Medicine and Health Sciences, exercising sound judgment, discretion, and independent decision-making in managing confidential correspondence, records, and communications. Develops, maintains, and analyzes databases, spreadsheets, and reports to support school operations, strategic planning, assessment, and institutional reporting. Assists with the preparation, organization, and management of materials supporting accreditation, institutional reporting, program review, and other compliance activities across the School of Medicine and Health Sciences. Serves as a professional and welcoming point of contact for students, faculty, staff, alumni, community partners, and visitors. Assists the Dean and Associate Dean with budget preparation, financial tracking, purchasing, reimbursements, and monitoring of school and departmental accounts. Collaborates with the Dean, Associate Dean, Program Directors, Department Chairs, faculty, and administrative staff to support school initiatives, improve operational efficiency, and achieve strategic goals. Coordinates logistics for meetings, retreats, accreditation visits, advisory boards, guest speakers, special events, and other school-sponsored activities, including scheduling, travel arrangements, and resource coordination. Assists with the development and maintenance of marketing materials, publications, website content, and other communications in collaboration with University Marketing and Communications. Coordinates space utilization and scheduling for School of Medicine and Health Sciences programs, meetings, and special events. Creates, updates, and maintains school and program forms, templates, procedural documents, and operational resources. Provides administrative support for faculty recruitment processes, including search committee logistics, candidate scheduling, and interview coordination. Coordinates with Facilities Management and Information Technology Services regarding maintenance, repairs, equipment needs, and technology support for the School of Medicine and Health Sciences. Maintains inventories of office supplies and coordinates purchasing for school administrative operations. Maintains records and databases related to faculty, adjunct faculty, staff, and other school personnel. Performs data entry, data retrieval, record management, and reporting to support school operations and decision-making. Serves as recording secretary for School of Medicine and Health Sciences meetings by coordinating schedules, preparing agendas, recording minutes, and distributing meeting materials in a timely manner. Perform other responsibilities that may be assigned by the Dean. Doctor of Executive Leadership Department Provides administrative support, including day-to-day program operations and coordination of faculty, student, and administrative activities. Serves as the primary administrative contact for prospective and current students, responding to inquiries and directing requests to appropriate faculty or university offices. Assists the Program Director with preparation of annual reports, assessment documentation, and other materials supporting institutional effectiveness, accreditation, and program review. Assists faculty with course administration, scheduling meetings, maintaining academic records, and coordinating adjunct faculty onboarding and support. Assists with the preparation and distribution of program communications, newsletters, marketing materials, and website content in collaboration with University Marketing and Admissions. Coordinates purchasing and inventory of office supplies and program materials and assists with budget tracking, purchase requests, reimbursements, and invoice processing. Collaborates with Information Technology Services to facilitate technology support for faculty, staff, and students and assists with troubleshooting program-related technology issues. Coordinates with Human Resources and Information Technology to facilitate onboarding of new faculty and staff, including office, computer, software, and system access. Maintains confidential student and program records in accordance with University policies and applicable federal regulations. Starting Salary: 35,000-42,000 Benefits: Generous paid vacation, personal days, paid sick time and family leave, comprehensive insurance (medical, dental, vision, etc.) and retirement plans, flexible spending account, tuition remission, life and long-term disability insurance, and more. Learn more about employment benefits at the University of Lynchburg. Schedule: Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Occasional evening and weekend hours may be required to support program activities, events, and operational needs. Qualifications Experience/Skills: Excellent written, verbal, organizational, and interpersonal communication skills. Strong interpersonal and customer service skills with the ability to provide professional, courteous, and responsive support to a diverse population of students, faculty, alumni, and prospective applicants. Excellent organizational and time management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities, meet deadlines, and maintain a high level of accuracy and attention to detail. Demonstrated ability to work independently while exercising sound judgment, discretion, and professionalism in handling confidential and sensitive information in accordance with University policies and FERPA. Experience coordinating multiple projects simultaneously, tracking deadlines, maintaining accurate records, and ensuring timely completion of administrative processes. Proficiency with Google Workspace (Docs, Sheets, Slides, Forms, Calendar, and Meet), with the ability to quickly learn and effectively utilize university systems and educational technologies. Experience working with learning management systems (e.g., Moodle, Canvas, Blackboard) and student information systems is preferred. Strong technology skills with the ability to support virtual meetings, online communications, and web-based collaboration platforms. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with faculty, administrators, students, and external partners while fostering a collaborative and service-oriented environment. Demonstrated problem-solving skills, initiative, and adaptability in a fast-paced academic environment with changing priorities. Ability to communicate effectively and have the ability to understand, comprehend and follow directions Must have good teamwork skills Physical Demands: Prolonged standing/sitting/wrist movement Ability to lift 10 lbs. Education: Associate's degree required; bachelor's degree preferred. Minimum of 5 years of progressively responsible administrative experience, preferably in a high-volume executive office or higher education setting. Work Remotely: No We seek candidates who are committed to the University of Lynchburg’s efforts to create an environment that fosters a student-centered environment, develops the breadth of knowledge associated with liberal education, respects and supports diversity, equity, and inclusion, values and celebrates diverse faith traditions, and sustains close working relationships among faculty, staff, students, alumni, and community partners. Candidates must successfully pass a background check that is satisfactory to the University. Submit a cover letter, résumé, and three professional references to: Human Resources Jobs Page The University of Lynchburg is dedicated to inclusive excellence. We celebrate the diversity of our common life, affirming our different histories, realities, and identities. All belong here. As a testament to our strong commitment to accessibility, diversity, and inclusion, we will attract, celebrate, and retain a community of diverse students, staff, and faculty; foster belonging; and create a campus environment that embraces civil discourse and accountability for our words and actions. The University of Lynchburg embraces diversity in its broadest sense. We will cultivate an inclusive, equitable, and safe campus climate grounded in mutual respect and understanding, where all members of our diverse learning community - alumni, employees, learners, visitors, and volunteers- can thrive. The University of Lynchburg is an equal-opportunity employer. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
