    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/06E60EB4A3425A1B8B2E3A5F3F1E2A6F/jobs/305917": {
      "title": "Director of Institutional Effectiveness",
      "description": "Director of Institutional Effectiveness You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Director of Institutional Effectiveness Lynchburg  - Lynchburg, VA 24501; Legal Address - Lynchburg, VA 24501 Apply Overview Salary Range $85,000.00 - $95,000.00 Salary Position Type Staff Job Shift Day Education Level Graduate Degree Apply Description Director of Institutional Effectiveness The University of Lynchburg , a private, regional university in the beautiful foothills of the Blue Ridge Mountains in Central Virginia, is seeking applicants for full-time Director of Institutional Effectiveness position in the Office of Institutional Effectiveness. This position reports to, is supervised by, and evaluated by the Vice President & Chief of Staff. The evaluation of work performance will be ongoing and will include the specific duties and responsibilities outlined in this position description, as well as employee attitude and general working behavior. Job Type : Full-time (Benefits Eligible) Job Purpose: The Director of Institutional Effectiveness leads the Office of Institutional Effectiveness (formerly University Data Analytics and Effectiveness) and is responsible for accreditation, institutional research, assessment, and data governance functions that support University of Lynchburg decision-making, planning, and compliance. The Director works closely with the Vice President & Chief of Staff and academic and administrative leaders across campus to ensure the University's data is accurate, well-governed, and used effectively to inform strategy. Specific Job Duties: Coordinates and supports the University's regional accreditation processes, reporting, and documentation, working in partnership with the University's Institutional Accreditation Liaison. Oversees the collection, analysis, and dissemination of institutional data to support planning, assessment, and evaluation of academic programs and University effectiveness. Ensures timely and accurate completion of federal, state, and other external reporting requirements (e.g., IPEDS, SCHEV, NCAA). Supervises the Coordinator of Institutional Research and other Institutional Effectiveness staff; participates in the recruitment, selection, and performance evaluation of unit personnel. Partners with the University Chief Information Officer (CIO) on data governance standards, data definitions, and the integrity of data feeding institutional dashboards and reports. Coordinates the development of program goals, objectives, policies, and standards for institutional data and effectiveness. Manages and maintains institutional dashboards and reporting tools used by University leadership. Responds to ad hoc requests for institutional data from campus leadership and external constituents. Serves on appropriate University standing and ad hoc committees. Manages the budget and daily operations of the Office of Institutional Effectiveness. Starting Salary: $85,000 – $95,000, commensurate with experience and qualifications. Benefits: Generous paid vacation, personal days, paid sick time and family leave, comprehensive insurance (medical, dental, vision, etc.) and retirement plans, flexible spending account, tuition remission, life and long-term disability insurance, and more. Learn more about employment benefits at the University of Lynchburg. Learn more about employment benefits at the University of Lynchburg. Schedule: 8:30 am - 5:00 pm (7.5 hours/day) with some evenings and weekends to meet needs of the department. Qualifications Experience/Skills: Strong communication skills, with the ability to identify and use appropriate and compelling data to contribute to effective decision-making. Ability to analyze and leverage data to promote institutional effectiveness, and to explain the use of data for the non-technical user. Awareness of trends in higher education that assist in strategic decision-making. Familiarity with multiple research and assessment platforms; understanding of data governance and data quality practices. Demonstrated ability to lead teams and collaborate across university units. Strong organizational and project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple deadlines. Physical Demands: Prolonged periods of sitting/standing and computer use. Frequent wrist and hand movement (typing, document handling). Ability to lift 15 lbs. Required Qualifications: Master's degree in a related field of study. 5–7 years of progressively responsible experience with data management, institutional research, or institutional effectiveness, preferably in higher education. Experience with accreditation processes and external compliance reporting. Proven ability to develop and maintain data architecture and dashboards across diverse institutional units. Familiarity with data visualization or query tools. Preferred qualifications: Terminal degree (e.g., PhD. or Ed.D.) in a related field such as higher education administration, institutional research, data science, or educational leadership. Direct experience with The Commission on Colleges and Universities (formerly SACSCOC) or another regional accrediting body. Experience supervising staff and managing a departmental budget. Education: Master's degree required Work Remotely: No We seek candidates who are committed to the University of Lynchburg’s efforts to create an environment that fosters a student-centered environment, develops the breadth of knowledge associated with liberal education, respects and supports diversity, equity, and inclusion, values and celebrates diverse faith traditions, and sustains close working relationships among faculty, staff, students, alumni, and community partners. Candidates must successfully pass a background check that is satisfactory to the University. Submit a cover letter, résumé, and three professional references to: Human Resources Jobs Page The University of Lynchburg is dedicated to inclusive excellence. We celebrate the diversity of our common life, affirming our different histories, realities, and identities. All belong here. As a testament to our strong commitment to accessibility, diversity, and inclusion, we will attract, celebrate, and retain a community of diverse students, staff, and faculty; foster belonging; and create a campus environment that embraces civil discourse and accountability for our words and actions. The University of Lynchburg embraces diversity in its broadest sense. We will cultivate an inclusive, equitable, and safe campus climate grounded in mutual respect and understanding, where all members of our diverse learning community - alumni, employees, learners, visitors, and volunteers- can thrive. The University of Lynchburg is an equal-opportunity employer. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/06E60EB4A3425A1B8B2E3A5F3F1E2A6F/jobs/303689": {
      "title": "Maintenance Technician-Carpentry",
      "description": "Maintenance Technician-Carpentry You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Maintenance Technician-Carpentry Lynchburg  - Lynchburg, VA 24501 Apply Overview Salary Range $21.00 - $22.00 Hourly Position Type Staff Job Shift Day Education Level High School Apply Description Maintenance Technician-Carpentry The University of Lynchburg , a private, regional university in the beautiful foothills of the Blue Ridge Mountains in Central Virginia, is seeking applicants for full-time Maintenance Technician position. This position reports to, is supervised by, and evaluated by the Director of Maintenance. The evaluation of work performance will be ongoing and will be carried out by the Maintenance Technician. It will include the specific duties and responsibilities of this position description plus employee attitude and general working behavior. Job Type : FT (Benefits Eligible) Job Purpose: Aligned with the mission of the Operations division, the Maintenance Technician – Carpentry is responsible for ensuring a safe, functional, and structurally sound campus environment. Working within a team of multi-disciplinary trades specialists (including electrical, plumbing, and HVAC), this position performs general campus-wide maintenance while serving as the university's primary expert for finish and structural carpentry, custom fabrications, and historic hardware preservation. Specific Job Duties: Specialized Carpentry & Fabrication: Lead the structural repair, alteration, and aesthetic maintenance of all campus facilities. Fabricate, install, and repair cabinetry, shelving, doors, frames, drywall, acoustic ceilings, and architectural trim across historic and modern university buildings. Cross-Functional Team Collaboration: Work dynamically within a multi-disciplinary team of \"specialists\" (including Electricians, Plumbers, and HVAC Technicians) to diagnose campus building issues and execute complex, multi-phase renovation or repair work orders seamlessly. General Maintenance Operations: Fulfill routine, daily general work orders assigned through the facilities management queue, performing basic preventative maintenance outside of the carpentry specialty when required by overall team volume and campus priorities. Hardware & Locking Systems: Troubleshoot, install, and maintain commercial door hardware, closers, exit devices, and related mechanical security components across academic and residential structures. Campus Event Logistics: Coordinate with the broader facilities management team to assist in the physical set-up, staging construction, and teardown for major university-wide milestones and events (e.g., Commencement, student move-in, and high-profile functions). Data-Driven Work Order Management: Utilize the university's Computerized Maintenance Management Systems (CMMS) to track, update, and close work orders, accurately logging labor hours, material costs, and structural diagnostic notes. Regulatory Compliance & Safety: Maintain strict adherence to all federal, state, and local safety regulations, including OSHA standards, fire/life safety codes, and proper personal protective equipment (PPE) protocols in the shop and in the field. Emergency Response & Severe Weather: Serve as essential personnel to execute severe weather protocols, including campus-wide snow and ice removal operations, and provide prompt response to after-hours structural or facilities emergencies. Starting Salary: $22.00 an hour Benefits: Generous paid vacation, personal days, paid sick time and family leave, comprehensive insurance (medical, dental, vision, etc.) and retirement plans, flexible spending account, tuition remission, life and long-term disability insurance, and more. Learn more about employment benefits at the University of Lynchburg. Schedule: 8:30 am - 5:00 pm- ( 7.5 hours/day with some evenings and weekends to meet needs of the department may be required. After hours response to facility emergencies and severe weather events.) Qualifications Experience/Skills: Technical Expertise: Advanced proficiency in reading blueprints, structural sketches, and technical drawings, alongside expert command of standard hand tools, power tools, and stationary shop machinery. Collaboration & Teamwork: Exceptional interpersonal skills with a proven track record of working effectively alongside peer specialists in other fields to achieve shared operational goals. Communication: Strong verbal and written communication skills to interact professionally with a diverse campus community, including faculty, staff, students, and external contractors. Problem Solving & Adaptability: Sound analytical skills to evaluate structural issues, calculate accurate material estimations, and pivot quickly to address building emergencies in a dynamic environment. Physical Demands: Working Conditions: Full-time, 100% on-site position. Requires standard daytime hours with the requirement to participate in a rotational on-call schedule for evening, weekend, or holiday hours; after hours response to facility emergencies and severe weather events. Physical Navigation: Active campus environment requiring daily physical navigation of multi-acre grounds, multi-story buildings without elevators, mechanical spaces, and active construction or repair zones. Physical Requirements: Ability to regularly lift and carry up to 50 pounds independently (and heavier loads with assistance); comfort working at heights on ladders, scaffolding, or aerial lifts; and the physical stamina to kneel, bend, and navigate confined spaces in varying temperatures and extreme weather conditions. Required Qualifications: Minimum of 3–5 years of progressive journeyman-level experience in commercial, residential, or institutional carpentry. Demonstrated experience working in a collaborative team environment alongside other core building trades (electrical, plumbing, or HVAC). Valid driver’s license with a clean motor vehicle record maintained throughout employment. Proficiency in using digital tools, mobile devices, or software platforms for tracking tasks or work requests. Preferred qualifications: Completion of a formal, recognized carpentry apprenticeship or a relevant trade school certification. Previous maintenance experience within a higher education campus, healthcare system, or similar large-scale institutional environment. Direct experience with commercial door hardware and locking systems. Completion of OSHA 10-hour or 30-hour safety training. Familiarity with the operational software platform Asset Essentials. Education: High school diploma or GED equivalent. Work Remotely: No We seek candidates who are committed to the University of Lynchburg’s efforts to create an environment that fosters a student-centered environment, develops the breadth of knowledge associated with liberal education, respects and supports diversity, equity, and inclusion, values and celebrates diverse faith traditions, and sustains close working relationships among faculty, staff, students, alumni, and community partners. Candidates must successfully pass a background check that is satisfactory to the University. Submit a cover letter, résumé, and three professional references to: Human Resources Jobs Page The University of Lynchburg is dedicated to inclusive excellence. We celebrate the diversity of our common life, affirming our different histories, realities, and identities. All belong here. As a testament to our strong commitment to accessibility, diversity, and inclusion, we will attract, celebrate, and retain a community of diverse students, staff, and faculty; foster belonging; and create a campus environment that embraces civil discourse and accountability for our words and actions. The University of Lynchburg embraces diversity in its broadest sense. We will cultivate an inclusive, equitable, and safe campus climate grounded in mutual respect and understanding, where all members of our diverse learning community - alumni, employees, learners, visitors, and volunteers- can thrive. The University of Lynchburg is an equal-opportunity employer. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/06E60EB4A3425A1B8B2E3A5F3F1E2A6F/jobs/303640": {
      "title": "Executive Director of Facilities Management",
      "description": "Executive Director of Facilities Management You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Executive Director of Facilities Management Lynchburg  - Lynchburg, VA 24501 Apply Overview Salary Range $100,000.00 - $120,000.00 Salary Position Type Staff Job Shift Day Education Level Graduate Degree Apply Description Executive Director of Facilities Management The University of Lynchburg , a private, regional university in the beautiful foothills of the Blue Ridge Mountains in Central Virginia, is seeking applicants for full-time, Executive Director of Facilities Management position in the Operations Department. This position reports to, is supervised by, and evaluated by the Assistant Vice President of Operations. The evaluation of work performance will be ongoing and will be carried out by the Executive Director of Facilities Management. It will include the specific duties and responsibilities of this position description plus employee attitude and general working behavior. Job Type : Full-time, Exempt, Benefits Eligible Job Purpose: The Executive Director of Facilities Management is a senior, 100% on-site leadership position responsible for overseeing the strategic direction, operational management, and physical development of the University's campus environment. This critical role requires a visionary, hands-on leader who can foster innovation, ensure the safety and functionality of the physical plant, manage multi-million dollar capital projects, and advance the university's mission while providing immediate, localized support to the presidential administration. The department encompasses Environmental Services & Grounds, Maintenance, Capital Projects, and Warehouse & Logistics (including vehicles, housing operations, and office moves) Specific Job Duties: Strategic Planning: Develop and implement comprehensive strategic plans for campus infrastructure and maintenance that align with the university’s goals and the new presidential administration's priorities. Leadership and Management: Provide executive leadership to the Facilities Management team. Directly supervise and mentor direct reports, and foster an inclusive, equitable work environment for a diverse workforce of tradespeople, staff, and contractors. Regulatory Compliance & Safety: Ensure strict campus compliance with all federal, state, and local regulations, including OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration), EPA (Environmental Protection Agency), ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act) accessibility standards, and fire/life safety codes. Policy Development: Formulate and implement policies for preventative maintenance, emergency response, and severe weather protocols to enhance operational effectiveness and ensure compliance with safety regulations. Budget Oversight: Manage complex departmental budgets, including the negotiation and oversight of external vendor contracts (e.g., landscaping, elevator maintenance, and waste management), resource allocation, and financial forecasting. Program Development & Sustainability: Oversee the creation of sustainable campus initiatives—prioritizing energy management, carbon footprint reduction, and waste diversion—alongside major capital renovations (including complex electrical infrastructure upgrades) and space management solutions. Housing Operations & Logistics: Direct comprehensive logistical operations, including the procurement and maintenance of the university vehicle fleet, execution of annual student move-in/move-out processes, and coordination of campus-wide faculty and staff office relocations. Collaboration and Advocacy: Serve as the primary liaison between Facilities Management and other university divisions (such as Residence Life, Campus Safety, and the Office of the President), fostering partnerships to execute seamless campus events and transitions. Data-Driven Decision Making: Utilize software tools and data analytics to evaluate work order efficiency, track preventative maintenance, and inform capital spending decisions. Community Engagement: Represent the university in local community relations, coordinating with city management and public works regarding zoning, comprehensive city plans, and major campus disruptions. Starting Salary: $100,000-$120,000 Benefits: Generous paid vacation, personal days, paid sick time and family leave, comprehensive insurance (medical, dental, vision, etc.) and retirement plans, flexible spending account, tuition remission, life and long-term disability insurance, and more. Learn more about employment benefits at the University of Lynchburg. Schedule: 8:30 am - 5:00 pm (7.5 hours/day with some evenings and weekends to meet needs of the department may be required) Qualifications Experience/Skills: Leadership: Exceptional leadership and team-building skills, with the ability to inspire and motivate a diverse workforce including tradespeople, project managers, and administrative staff. Communication: Outstanding verbal and written communication skills, capable of conveying complex technical and construction details clearly to non-technical audiences, including executive leadership and external stakeholders. Analytical Thinking: Strong analytical and critical thinking skills to assess emergency situations, identify infrastructure challenges, and implement cost-effective solutions. Interpersonal Skills: Ability to build and maintain positive, collaborative relationships across all levels of the university. Adaptability: Flexibility to pivot and direct emergency responses 24/7 in a dynamic higher education environment. Physical Demands: Working Conditions: Full-time, 100% on-site position requiring standard office hours with frequent evening, weekend, or on-call commitments to respond to campus emergencies, severe weather events, or major campus milestones (e.g., Commencement, homecoming, student move-in, founder’s week). Physical Navigation: Active campus environment requiring regular physical navigation of multi-acre grounds, mechanical rooms, and active construction sites, alongside standard office interactions. Physical Requirements: The ability to lift and carry up to 50 pounds, safely climb ladders, navigate confined spaces, and endure exposure to varying temperatures and extreme weather conditions during site inspections and emergencies. Required Qualifications: Minimum of 7-10 years of progressive leadership experience in facilities management or physical plant operations, with demonstrated success in team leadership, capital project management, and strategic planning. Proven experience in complex budget management, vendor contract negotiation, and resource allocation. Proficiency in utilizing Computerized Maintenance Management Systems (CMMS) to drive operational efficiency. Preferred qualifications: Experience in a senior administrative facilities role within a university, healthcare system, or similar large-scale institutional environment. Professional certifications such as Certified Facility Manager (CFM), Certified Educational Facilities Professional (CEFP), or a Professional Engineer (P.E.) license. Completion of OSHA 10-hour or 30-hour safety training. Familiarity with current trends, sustainability challenges, and technological operations (e.g., HVAC, switchgear, plumbing systems) within higher education. Direct experience with specific operational software platforms, including Asset Essentials and StarRez. Education: Bachelor’s degree in Engineering, Facilities Management, Business Administration, or a closely related field. or Master’s degree in Higher Education Administration, Business Administration, or a related field. Work Remotely: No We seek candidates who are committed to the University of Lynchburg’s efforts to create an environment that fosters a student-centered environment, develops the breadth of knowledge associated with liberal education, respects and supports diversity, equity, and inclusion, values and celebrates diverse faith traditions, and sustains close working relationships among faculty, staff, students, alumni, and community partners. Candidates must successfully pass a background check that is satisfactory to the University. Submit a cover letter, résumé, and three professional references to: Human Resources Jobs Page The University of Lynchburg is dedicated to inclusive excellence. We celebrate the diversity of our common life, affirming our different histories, realities, and identities. All belong here. As a testament to our strong commitment to accessibility, diversity, and inclusion, we will attract, celebrate, and retain a community of diverse students, staff, and faculty; foster belonging; and create a campus environment that embraces civil discourse and accountability for our words and actions. The University of Lynchburg embraces diversity in its broadest sense. We will cultivate an inclusive, equitable, and safe campus climate grounded in mutual respect and understanding, where all members of our diverse learning community - alumni, employees, learners, visitors, and volunteers- can thrive. The University of Lynchburg is an equal-opportunity employer. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/06E60EB4A3425A1B8B2E3A5F3F1E2A6F/jobs/299434": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Physical Therapy (Neuromuscular Specialist Preferred)",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Physical Therapy (Neuromuscular Specialist Preferred) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant/Associate Professor of Physical Therapy (Neuromuscular Specialist Preferred) Lynchburg  - Lynchburg, VA 24501 Apply Overview Salary Range $85,000.00 - $100,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Faculty Job Shift Full time Education Level Graduate Degree Apply Description The University of Lynchburg, a private, regional university in the beautiful foothills of the Blue Ridge Mountains in Central Virginia, is seeking applicants for a full-time faculty position in the Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) Program starting at the beginning of the 2026-2027 academic year. Salary and rank will correspond to experience and educational credentials. The DPT Program is part of the School of Medicine and Health Sciences with opportunities for interprofessional experiences with a variety of other health science programs. The program is housed in the Graduate Health Sciences Building with more than 37,000 square feet dedicated to physical therapy instruction, service, and research. The curriculum features an innovative model of instruction that prepares student physical therapists to become generalist practitioners who become leaders in the profession. Clinical practice is promoted among faculty and opportunities exist within the onsite free clinic. The Program received initial accreditation in 2013 and is scheduled for re-review in 2028. Specific Job Duties: Teaching courses in the DPT Program Collaborating with colleagues on curriculum development, supervising student research projects, service to the University and community, and engaging in scholarly activity Applying best practices to facilitate teaching and learning processes and principles with a commitment to continuous quality improvement Documenting student learning, interpreting outcomes, and recording grades Assisting with student recruitment, admission, and retention Maintaining accurate and appropriate student, instructor, course, and program documentation Establishing and maintaining professional and ethical boundaries with students, co-workers, and others in all learning environments Participating in University service and events Perform other responsibilities that may be assigned by the DPT Program Director and Dean School of Medicine and Health Sciences Benefits: Generous sick time and family leave, comprehensive insurance (medical, dental, vision, etc.) and retirement plans, flexible spending account, tuition remission, life and long-term disability insurance, and more. Learn more about employment benefits at the University of Lynchburg . Teaching Load: Full-time faculty members are expected to teach the equivalent of 12 credit hours per semester. Salary: $85,000-$100,000 Physical Demands: Prolonged periods standing or sitting, typical physical demands of a physical therapist in a clinical setting. Position Description: The DPT at the University of Lynchburg invites applications for a full-time (12 month) tenure track or non-tenure track assistant/associate professor level faculty position to begin during the Summer or Fall of 2026. Individuals with a terminal academic degree may be eligible for tenure track Qualifications Required Qualifications/Education: For individuals with a terminal academic degree (e.g. PhD, EdD, DSc, or DHSc), at least a Master’s degree in physical therapy is required; candidates approaching completion of a terminal academic degree may also be considered For individuals without a terminal academic degree, a Doctor of Physical Therapy degree and an APTA Specialist Certification (governed by ABPTS) is required; highly qualified individuals eligible to sit for APTA Specialist Certification may also be considered Experience teaching entry-level content to DPT students A minimum of three years of contemporary physical therapy clinical practice Strong communication and interpersonal skills and the ability to collaborate with colleagues Licensed or eligible for licensure as a physical therapist in the Commonwealth of Virginia (Virginia licensure is required within one year of employment) A scholarly agenda that contributes to teaching and/or practice The ability and credentials to teach courses related to neuromuscular practice Work Remotely: No Candidates may show interest in this position by submitting to the Human Resources Jobs Page . Applications must include the following: A completed application A cover letter to include a statement of your Teaching Philosophy with a statement on your approach to diversity, equity, and inclusion in teaching. A current curriculum vitae (CV) or resume During the application review process, candidates may be asked to provide the following: Graduate and undergraduate transcripts (unofficial transcripts accepted; however, official transcripts are required upon an offer and acceptance of position) Names and contact information for three professional references To ensure full consideration, completed applications must be received by August 15, 2026. Review of applications and materials will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. The selected candidate must successfully complete a background check that is satisfactory to the University. The University of Lynchburg is dedicated to inclusive excellence. We celebrate the diversity of our common life, affirming our different histories, realities, and identities. All belong here. As a testament to our strong commitment to accessibility, diversity, and inclusion, we will attract, celebrate, and retain a community of diverse students, staff, and faculty; foster belonging; and create a campus environment that embraces civil discourse and accountability for our words and actions. The University of Lynchburg embraces diversity in its broadest sense. We will cultivate an inclusive, equitable, and safe campus climate grounded in mutual respect and understanding, where all members of our diverse learning community - alumni, employees, learners, visitors, and volunteers- can thrive. The University of Lynchburg is an equal-opportunity employer Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/06E60EB4A3425A1B8B2E3A5F3F1E2A6F/jobs/264246": {
      "title": "Athletics Student Assistant (Dell Mascot)",
      "description": "Athletics Student Assistant (Dell Mascot) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Athletics Student Assistant (Dell Mascot) Lynchburg  - Lynchburg, VA 24501 Apply Overview Position Type Student Job Shift Part time Education Level None Apply Description Become a member of The Dell Crew. The Dell Crew’s mission is to embody the spirit, tradition, and excitement of the University of Lynchburg and its athletic programs through the energetic and charismatic representation of our mascot, Dell the Hornet. The Dell Crew will enhance school pride, promote fan engagement, and represent the University at games, campus events, and community activities. Members will rotate responsibilities as our campus mascot, Dell, and the handler/assistant. Roles and responsibilities include wearing the Dell mascot costume, performing, interacting with fans, and upholding the character's persona. The secondary role as handler/assistant includes assisting with costume, escorting Dell, ensuring performer safety, and facilitating fan interaction. Dell Mascot Key Responsibilities: Performance: Bring Dell the Hornet to life through non-verbal communication, consistent high energy, and engaging movement (e.g., dancing, stunts, skits). Character Maintenance: Uphold the established personality of Dell—friendly, spirited, mischievous, and a symbol of Hornet pride. Event Participation: Perform at scheduled University events, including home football/soccer (as applicable), basketball, and select other athletic contests, as well as campus and community appearances. Costume Care: Handle and clean the Dell costume according to guidelines to ensure its longevity and readiness. Dell Handler/Assistant Key Responsibilities: Safety & Logistics: Serve as the mascot's eyes and ears, guiding Dell around venues, ensuring performer safety, and managing time-outs/breaks. Fan Facilitation: Assist with fan interactions, distributing small giveaways, taking photos, and managing crowds around the mascot. Costume Transportation: Assist in the transport and preparation of the Dell costume and props before and after events. Support: Serve as a backup performer, if qualified and needed, during emergencies or if a performer is unavailable. Qualifications Dell Mascot Qualifications: Must be a currently enrolled, full-time University of Lynchburg student in good academic standing. Physical stamina, flexibility, and a tolerance for heat. Excellent non-verbal communication and crowd interaction skills. Reliability, professionalism, and the ability to maintain the secrecy of the Dell identity. Dell Handler/Assistant Qualifications: Must be a currently enrolled, full-time University of Lynchburg student in good academic standing. Strong organizational and communication skills. Alertness, responsibility, and the ability to work in a fast-paced environment. Try-Out Process and Criteria Tryouts will be held annually, typically in the spring, with a supplemental round in the fall if positions remain open. A. Eligibility: Full-time University of Lynchburg student status. Minimum cumulative GPA of 2.5 (or as determined by the University). Completed application and required liability/medical release forms. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/06E60EB4A3425A1B8B2E3A5F3F1E2A6F/jobs/96638": {
      "title": "Adjunct Nursing Clinical Faculty",
      "description": "Adjunct Nursing Clinical Faculty You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Nursing Clinical Faculty Apply Overview Position Type Faculty Job Shift Part time Education Level Graduate Degree Apply Description University of Lynchburg School of Nursing is seeking applicants for adjunct positions to teach clinical courses beginning in October and January. Day and Evening clinical assignments are available. Qualifications Requirements: Master's Degree in Nursing required RN licensure in state of Virginia or Compact state required Proof of License will be required at time of employment Employment is contingent upon satisfactory background check. Transcripts must be submitted to be considered for review. Unofficial transcripts or a copy of the transcript is acceptable for application purposes. Official transcripts will be required upon hire.  Cover letter should address areas of specialty and availability. The University of Lynchburg is committed to diversity within its community and welcomes applications from persons of color, women, Indigenous/aboriginal people of North America, persons with disabilities, the LGBTQIA+ community, and others who may contribute to the further diversification of the University of Lynchburg community. The University of Lynchburg is an equal opportunity employer. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/06E60EB4A3425A1B8B2E3A5F3F1E2A6F/jobs/310539": {
      "title": "Campus Safety and Security Officer",
      "description": "Campus Safety and Security Officer You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Campus Safety and Security Officer Lynchburg  - Lynchburg, VA 24501 Apply Overview Salary Range $17.00 - $19.00 Hourly Position Type Staff Job Shift Full time Education Level High School Apply Description Campus Security Officer The University of Lynchburg , a private, regional university in the beautiful foothills of the Blue Ridge Mountains in Central Virginia, is seeking applicants for full-time, Campus Security Officer position. This position reports to, is supervised by, and evaluated by the Campus Security Supervisor/and Director of Campus Security. The evaluation of work performance will be ongoing and will be carried out by the Campus Security Officer. It will include the specific duties and responsibilities of this position description plus employee attitude and general working behavior. Job Type : Full time Benefits Eligible Job Purpose: To provide and assist in the immediate protection and security of students, faculty, staff and visitors in various campus buildings and/or property within the university community by enforcing the policies and procedures set by the university, state, and local laws. Specific Job Duties: Respond to all calls for service in a timely and professional manner. Conduct investigations as required and document findings in accordance with department policies and procedures. Provide security and protective services to the campus community through routine patrols of assigned buildings, parking areas, and grounds. Respond to emergency situations by assessing conditions, exercising sound judgment, and using tact and diplomacy to maintain safety and restore order. Complete incident reports and other required documentation accurately and promptly. Maintain continuous radio communication with the dispatcher and other department personnel. Provide crowd management and traffic control during campus events, special activities, and emergency situations. Provide authorized access to campus buildings and verify the identity and authorization of individuals requesting entry. Identify safety hazards during patrols and promptly submit work orders or notify the appropriate university personnel for corrective action. Patrol campus parking areas to ensure compliance with parking regulations and issue citations when appropriate. Monitor fire lanes to ensure they remain unobstructed and take appropriate enforcement action in accordance with university policy. Provide safety escorts to students, faculty, staff, and visitors in a timely and professional manner. Maintain a thorough knowledge of campus facilities, roadways, parking areas, and university operations to effectively respond to calls for service. Assist with the training and mentoring of newly assigned officers as directed by the training supervisor. Provide relief staffing for the Control Center as assigned. Secure campus buildings during assigned shifts by conducting routine security inspections of doors, windows, mechanical systems, and other critical building components. Contact Facilities Management or other appropriate personnel to coordinate emergency repairs or address maintenance-related concerns. Attend and successfully complete all required professional development, certifications, and in-service training. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Starting Salary: $17.00-$19.00 an hour Benefits: Generous paid vacation, personal days, paid sick time and family leave, comprehensive insurance (medical, dental, vision, etc.) and retirement plans, flexible spending account, tuition remission, life and long-term disability insurance, and more. Learn more about employment benefits at the University of Lynchburg. Schedule: Shift will include evenings or overnights to meet needs of the department. Experience/Skills: Ability to communicate effectively and have the ability to understand, comprehend and follow directions Must have good teamwork skills Entry Level (Prior Law Enforcement, security, or military experience preferred). Physical Demands: Prolonged standing/setting/wrist movement Prolonged walking significant distances between and within building on campus often in adverse weather conditions. Ability to lift 50lbs. Qualifications Required Qualifications: Strong verbal and written communication skills. Ability to read, interpret, and follow printed materials, instructions, and procedures. Ability to remain calm under pressure, respond appropriately in emergency situations, and communicate effectively with the appropriate authorities. Strong attention to detail and the ability to accurately recall events for incident and report documentation. Proficiency with basic computer applications and general computer skills. Preferred qualifications: CPR Certified AED Certified Education: High school diploma or equivalent education Certified by the State of Virginia Department of Criminal Justice Services as a CSO within 180 days of employment Valid Virginia State Vehicle Operator's License Work Remotely: No We seek candidates who are committed to the University of Lynchburg’s efforts to create an environment that fosters a student-centered environment, develops the breadth of knowledge associated with liberal education, respects and supports diversity, equity, and inclusion, values and celebrates diverse faith traditions, and sustains close working relationships among faculty, staff, students, alumni, and community partners. Candidates must successfully pass a background check that is satisfactory to the University. Submit a cover letter, résumé, and three professional references to: Human Resources Jobs Page The University of Lynchburg is dedicated to inclusive excellence. We celebrate the diversity of our common life, affirming our different histories, realities, and identities. All belong here. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/06E60EB4A3425A1B8B2E3A5F3F1E2A6F/jobs/310527": {
      "title": "Website Manager & Content Strategist",
      "description": "Website Manager & Content Strategist You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Website Manager & Content Strategist Lynchburg  - Lynchburg, VA 24501 Apply Overview Salary Range $62,000.00 - $68,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Staff Job Shift Full time Education Level 4 Year Degree Apply Description Website Manager & Content Strategist The University of Lynchburg , a private, regional university in the beautiful foothills of the Blue Ridge Mountains in Central Virginia, is seeking applicants for full-time, Website Manager position in the Department of Marketing and Communications. This position reports to, is supervised by, and evaluated by the Executive Director of Marketing. The evaluation of work performance will be ongoing and will be carried out by the Website Manager and Content Strategist. It will include the specific duties and responsibilities of this position description plus employee attitude and general working behavior. Job Type : FT (Benefits Eligible) Job Purpose: The Website Manager & Content Strategist is the technical and editorial owner of the University of Lynchburg's digital presence. This is a strategic role responsible for the intersection of content strategy, web performance, and AI-driven discoverability. The Website Manager ensures our digital platforms serve prospective students, current students, faculty, and the broader community with clarity and speed, while serving as the bridge between creative marketing goals and technical execution. Specific Job Duties: Develop and own the University's web content strategy, including voice, structure, and editorial standards across all digital platforms. Build and enforce a centralized content intake and governance model to manage requests from departments across the University. Execute hands-on website updates and page builds using WordPress and Elementor, reorganizing content for web best practices and audience clarity. Audit, map, and continuously improve site navigation and information architecture to reduce friction for prospective students and other key audiences. Manage the WP Engine hosting environment, including staging and production workflows, server-side performance optimization, and plugin governance. Establish and maintain global Elementor templates and design guidelines to ensure a cohesive brand presence across all web platforms. Ensure 100% of site content meets WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility standards and own the annual audit and remediation process. Optimize content for both traditional organic search and AI-discovery engines, including structured data, FAQ strategy, and entity-based content approaches. Own GA4 implementation and deliver monthly analytics reports to leadership connecting web performance to enrollment funnel metrics. Identify and implement AI-assisted tools to accelerate content production, metadata generation, and A/B testing while maintaining brand and accuracy standards Maintain and develop an editorial calendar aligned to the academic year, admissions cycle, and University events. Supervise the student Digital Media Assistant and serve as a mentor for emerging web and content professionals. Collaborate across departments via Asana, email, and Google Workspace while enforcing centralized governance standards. Starting Salary: $62,000-$68,000 Benefits: Generous paid vacation, personal days, paid sick time and family leave, comprehensive insurance (medical, dental, vision, etc.) and retirement plans, flexible spending account, tuition remission, life and long-term disability insurance, and more. Learn more about employment benefits at the University of Lynchburg. Schedule: 8:30 am - 5:00 pm (7.5 hours/day with some evenings and weekends to meet needs of the department may be required) Qualifications Experience/Skills: Minimum of 5 year of progressive experience in website management, digital content strategy, or web marketing, preferably in higher education or a mission-driven organization. Demonstrated experience owning a large, multi-stakeholder website (500+pages) from both a strategic and technical standpoint. Proven track record of developing and executing a content strategy that improved measurable outcomes such as traffic, leads, time-on-site, or enrollment inquires. Background working in environments with decentralized content contributors and centralized governance, ideally in higher education, healthcare, or government. Advanced, hands-on experience with WordPress and Elementor, including custom CSS, template hierarchy, and plugin management. Proficiency with WP Engine's hosting platform, staging environments, CDN configuration, and performance tooling. Working expertise in technical SEO, including Core Web Vitals, schema markup, canonical tags, and XML sitemaps. Solid working knowledge of HTML and CSS sufficient to write and debug custom code within WordPress. Experience auditing and remediating WCAG 2.1 AA issues using tools such as Siteimprove, axe, or WAVE. Familiarity with AI writing assistants and emerging LLM-powered content tools such as Gemini, Notebook LM, ChatGPT, Claude, Jasper, or Surfer SEO. Experience with project management and intake tools such as Asana, Monday.com, or similar platforms. Strong written communication skills and ability to enforce editorial standards across a large organization. Physical Demands: Prolonged sitting and wrist movement Required Qualifications: Minimum of 5 years of experience in website management or digital content strategy. Advanced proficiency in WordPress and Elementor. Demonstrated knowledge of SEO best practices and GA4 analytics. Working knowledge of WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility standards. Preferred qualifications: Experience in a higher education marketing or communications environment, with fluency in the enrollment funnel as it applies to prospective students. Familiarity with CRM integrations such as Slate or Salesforce and how web forms connect to enrollment systems. Experience with heatmap and UX research tools such as Hotjar or Microsoft Clarity. Working knowledge of email marketing platforms and how web content connects to audience nurture campaigns. Experience with AI-powered SEO tools such as Surfer, Clearscope, or SEMrush AI, and an understanding of how large language models surface institutional content. Background in brand management or experience maintaining a design system or style guide at scale. Certifications in Google Analytics, HubSpot Content, or a recognized SEO platform. Experience with video, podcast, or multimedia content strategy as the University expands its content formats. Education: Bachelor's Degree in Communication, Marketing, Journalism, Information Science, or a related field. Equivalent experience may be considered. Work Remotely: No We seek candidates who are committed to the University of Lynchburg’s efforts to create an environment that fosters a student-centered environment, develops the breadth of knowledge associated with liberal education, respects and supports diversity, equity, and inclusion, values and celebrates diverse faith traditions, and sustains close working relationships among faculty, staff, students, alumni, and community partners. Candidates must successfully pass a background check that is satisfactory to the University. Submit a cover letter, résumé, and three professional references to: Human Resources Jobs Page The University of Lynchburg is dedicated to inclusive excellence. We celebrate the diversity of our common life, affirming our different histories, realities, and identities. All belong here. As a testament to our strong commitment to accessibility, diversity, and inclusion, we will attract, celebrate, and retain a community of diverse students, staff, and faculty; foster belonging; and create a campus environment that embraces civil discourse and accountability for our words and actions. The University of Lynchburg embraces diversity in its broadest sense. We will cultivate an inclusive, equitable, and safe campus climate grounded in mutual respect and understanding, where all members of our diverse learning community - alumni, employees, learners, visitors, and volunteers- can thrive. The University of Lynchburg is an equal-opportunity employer. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    }
